<title>LATVIA: Latvia expected to get S&amp;P rating.</title>
<headline>Latvia expected to get S&amp;P rating.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Latvia is to get a credit rating by Standard &amp; Poor's, the second Baltic country to get a rating after Lithuania was awarded one by Moody's, a local news agency said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The Baltic News Service (BNS) quoted the spokesman for Prime Minister Andris Shkele as saying S&amp;P would release the credit rating next week. The spokesman would not reveal what the rating would be, the agency said.</p>
<p>Moody's rated Lithuania's foreign currency debt as Ba2 and its bank deposits at Ba3. Lithuania is also expecting to get a rating by IBCA.</p>
<p>-- Riga Newsroom, +371 721 5240</p>
</text>
